{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/l7k5j9","slideIndex":0,"text":"Target impact, not measured clinical or deployment results. Fifteen to two minutes is an 86.7% reduction in entry time, rounded to 87%, not an 87% increase in entry speed. 100% refers to the proposed digitization target, not proven nationwide record availability. Thirty seconds is a QR access target. Self-learning describes the proposed doctor-approval feedback loop; automatic learning and daily improvement are not demonstrated. The 40% consultation-time reduction was not included because no supporting evaluation was supplied. NFC retrieves an identifier and looks up the associated record; it does not extract clinical history from the wristband. PN532 is the NFC reader; ESP32-C3 is its controller. Both images are AI-generated illustrations, not actual prototype or deployment photographs. Photo and voice outputs must be reviewed by the doctor before QR handoff."}